WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.650
- There's a moment where you

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.450
and your sisters sing in Pig Latin.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:04.283
- Oh yeah!

00:00:04.283 --> 00:00:05.130
- Which I love.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.170
Is this something that
y'all, y'all do all the time?

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.790
- No, we don't do it all the time.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.980
I had learned Pig Latin
when I was in school.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:11.813
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:11.813 --> 00:00:13.937
And I used to just, I
would just beg my sisters

00:00:13.937 --> 00:00:16.530
I'd do their chores, I'd
do everything I could

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.690
to get them to work up stuff with me.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:19.840
So I had the big idea to

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.909
to have back, background in Pig Latin.

00:00:22.909 --> 00:00:26.760
So I'd written a song called
The Friendliest Enemies

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.050
like she's the friendliest enemy,

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:29.160
I believe ever did see her.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.260
And she'd better get my baby off of mine.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.760
And it's like she was my best friend.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.059
So, the Pig Latin part
was where they were going.

00:00:35.059 --> 00:00:38.310
It's the Pig Latin says
she was my best friend.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.669
So oh, eiche, os sway.

00:00:40.669 --> 00:00:42.859
I may, espe and pray.

00:00:42.859 --> 00:00:47.550
eiche, os sway, I may, espe and pray ooh.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:49.410
She's the friendly cinnamon.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.000
Then they would come in on the parts

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.138
where it was background.

00:00:52.138 --> 00:00:53.004
- I love that!

00:00:53.004 --> 00:00:54.090
- [Dolly] So, and we did it on the show.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:54.923
And harmonies.

00:00:54.923 --> 00:00:56.103
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:00:56.103 --> 00:00:56.936
My sister Cassie and Rachel.

00:00:56.936 --> 00:00:58.620
And then I had a lot of
my family on the show.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.810
So, uh, we're singing in Pig Latin.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:01.643
- I know.

00:01:01.643 --> 00:01:02.610
I just love that you can like burn someone

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:03.570
and they don't even know what's happening.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:04.403
Cause it's in Pig Latin.

00:01:04.403 --> 00:01:06.660
Like, it's like I'm totally
gonna steal the idea.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.607
I was like, they don't even
know what you're saying.

00:01:08.607 --> 00:01:09.600
Really. So, did you say it?

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.010
- I can't even say it (bleep).

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:11.843
- Yeah.

00:01:11.843 --> 00:01:15.210
(laughs) (claps hands)

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:16.780
- Well, you can keep it classy.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.330
I'll, I'll keep it.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:19.290
I won't be.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.450
Um, is it true that
you wrote a secret song

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.580
that nobody else has ever heard

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:24.810
and you put it in a time capsule?

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.750
- Yes. And that has drove me crazy

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.980
- Because people bring it up?

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:29.813
- No. Yeah.

00:01:29.813 --> 00:01:30.646
Because they bring it up.

00:01:30.646 --> 00:01:33.510
But because I have written a
song that nobody's going to

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.790
hear till I'm 99 years old.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.088
And I might be there, I might not be.

00:01:38.088 --> 00:01:41.970
But it's when we did
Dollywood, when we worked that.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:42.803
- Yeah.

00:01:42.803 --> 00:01:44.430
- And we put it in a time capsule to be,

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.140
you know, to be opened.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:46.973
It wasn't.

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:48.499
- To kind of honor the old opening. Yeah.

00:01:48.499 --> 00:01:50.430
- Yeah. And so, and I put all the things

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.200
that had to do with the times.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.977
I put a cassette player and
I put a, all the CD player

00:01:56.977 --> 00:01:57.810
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:01.520
I put stuff all in this box
that if, if it would preserve it

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.848
to what, how we played
those, you know, at the time.

00:02:03.848 --> 00:02:04.681
- Yeah.

00:02:04.681 --> 00:02:07.110
- [Dolly] But I put that
in the box, but I had to

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:10.717
write this song that nobody
was going to hear till then.

00:02:10.717 --> 00:02:14.910
And I tell you have no idea
how that has bothered me.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.768
I wanna go dig that up so bad and think

00:02:16.768 --> 00:02:19.320
well I need to use that song.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:22.170
Cause it's like, you know,
and it's a really good song.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:23.003
But yes.

00:02:23.003 --> 00:02:25.590
I, I have a song that's buried

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.390
that nobody's going hear till.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.317
Till, I don't know whose
damn idea that was.

00:02:29.317 --> 00:02:30.150
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.470
You're like, I'm like when's the cutoff.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:32.430
Is there a date?

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:33.263
Do you know?

00:02:33.263 --> 00:02:35.310
We need to find the date
till we get to unearth it.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:38.149
- So I'm 76 and it's
when I'm 99 years old.

00:02:38.149 --> 00:02:39.450
- It is when you're 99.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:42.330
- Yeah. I'd be 99 years old
when they, when they open it.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:43.163
Yeah.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.519
- God, you got like a lot more
time to wait for that one.

00:02:45.519 --> 00:02:46.510
(laughs)

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:47.343
- I know, but I, they

00:02:47.343 --> 00:02:49.650
they weren't expecting
me to be there at all.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:50.483
And they, and I thought

00:02:50.483 --> 00:02:51.615
- Well, that's just rude.

00:02:51.615 --> 00:02:52.488
- [Dolly] Probably won't be.

00:02:52.488 --> 00:02:53.321
(laughs)

00:02:53.321 --> 00:02:54.154
- [Kelly] That's just rude.

00:02:54.154 --> 00:02:56.880
- But I mean, I'm just saying
I might be there, who knows?

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.250
But the point is, that there is a, a song

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.810
I figure it'd probably disintegrate.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.010
Probably nobody ever hear it.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:03.600
That's what bothers me to think.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.433
- Oh.

00:03:04.433 --> 00:03:06.240
- That it's gonna be a song
that nobody's ever going

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.973
to hear if it rots in there
before, before they open it.

00:03:08.973 --> 00:03:10.800
- What a beautiful thing
though, when they open it.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.890
What a, what a beautiful thing.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:14.670
I, I love, I'm totally

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.370
and I've done time capsule gifts before.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:18.203
More as a joke.

00:03:18.203 --> 00:03:20.610
Like, I gave Blake Shelton a time capsule

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:22.350
for his birthday last year to open it,

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:23.250
the one this year.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.816
And it was just like my team
Kelly jacket from The Voice

00:03:25.816 --> 00:03:27.808
(laughs)

00:03:27.808 --> 00:03:29.010
and like, cuz he kept throwing it away.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.390
And I was like, you've
had this for a year.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:31.230
Jokes on you.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.390
So, but anyway, I've
done it in a funny way

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:34.560
but I've never done it in a serious way.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.730
And I think that's almost beautiful too

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.320
for like people to do,
for like their kids.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.490
Like make something for their kids.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:39.660
If you can't sing, like make a video

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.070
and like have 'em
unearth it at some point.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.360
I think that's really special.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.090
- Well, it'll be, hopefully
it'll be special and hopefully

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.019
it'll still be there.

00:03:46.019 --> 00:03:47.569
(laughs)

00:03:47.569 --> 00:03:49.008
- Ya'll enjoy it.

00:03:49.008 --> 00:03:51.117
- [Dolly] Some of you might
be, some of you might not.

00:03:51.117 --> 00:03:51.950
- [Kelly] Oh, I gotta learn.

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:52.783
- But it is true though.

00:03:52.783 --> 00:03:54.870
But it's an odd feeling,
I have to honestly say

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:55.703
it was a odd feeling.

00:03:55.703 --> 00:03:56.536
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:57.369
- To be asked to write a song

00:03:57.369 --> 00:03:59.379
that nobody was not, not going to hear it.

00:03:59.379 --> 00:04:00.840
I mean, it was not gonna be heard.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:01.980
- That is annoying.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:02.813
It is. Yeah.

00:04:02.813 --> 00:04:03.646
- [Dolly] Yeah.

00:04:03.646 --> 00:04:04.742
But it's a good song.

00:04:04.742 --> 00:04:06.192
- Oh, well we, we don't know.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.180
- Yes. No you don't.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:11.130
But I mean, I felt like it was
a good song and I think, oh

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:13.230
I don't know if this, maybe
I'll write a bad song.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.063
I'll put it in there.

00:04:14.063 --> 00:04:15.180
Who's gonna remember me then?

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.760
- Yeah. You should have done
it like a more of a joke,

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:18.870
like jokes on you.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:19.950
You thought this was gonna be great.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:21.248
- [Dolly] That's right. Yeah. (laughs)

00:04:21.248 --> 00:04:22.081
- Nope. You shoulda called it, nope.

00:04:22.081 --> 00:04:23.250
- That's what I'm going to do now.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:24.480
I'm gonna go dig that up and put

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.693
- Bury that right beside
it and get the other one.

